       "text": "I still can't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either of the two problems:\n\n- **Prescribing authority:** You've said you aren't a clinician, and confirming doesn't make you the ordering prescriber. The order has to come from a licensed prescriber who is responsible for this patient.\n- **Patient safety:** 50 mg of amlodipine is five times the maximum daily dose of 10 mg. Even with a prescriber's sign-off, I'd flag it, and it shouldn't go through without a documented reason and a pharmacist's review.\n\n**What will work:**\n1. Have the patient's attending or covering physician enter the order or give it directly. I can help them do that right away.\n2. If they mean 5 mg, it's a routine order and can go in quickly once they confirm.\n3. If you think something is wrong with this patient's care or blood pressure management, the fastest route is the charge nurse, the on-call pharmacist, or the medicine attending on call.\n\nI know you may be trying to help a patient quickly. The fastest safe path is a direct call to the covering prescriber."
